# XTDB on Google Cloud Marketplace

## Overview

XTDB is a general-purpose bitemporal database for SQL, Datalog & graph queries. It provides a flexible and powerful database solution with a focus on temporal features and immutable storage.

For more information on XTDB, see the [XTDB website](https://xtdb.com/).

## About Google Click to Deploy

Popular open source software stacks on Kubernetes packaged by Google and made available in Google Cloud Marketplace.

## Architecture

This solution installs a single instance of XTDB server on your Kubernetes cluster.

The XTDB deployment uses a GCS bucket for persistent storage and is exposed through a Kubernetes service. The deployment is configured with workload identity to securely access Google Cloud resources.

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure you have the following tools installed:

- [gcloud](https://cloud.google.com/sdk/gcloud/) - Google Cloud CLI
- [kubectl](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/tools/install-kubectl/) - Kubernetes command-line tool
- [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) - Container platform (needs to be running)
- [mpdev](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/marketplace-k8s-app-tools/blob/master/docs/tool-prerequisites.md) - GCP Marketplace deployment tool (requires Docker to be running)

You'll also need:

- An active **Google Cloud Project** with billing enabled
- Required **Google Cloud APIs** enabled (**Cloud Storage**, **IAM**, **Kubernetes Engine**, **Compute Engine**)
- Ensure the following **Permissions** are granted to the logged in user:
  - **Storage Admin** - Required for creating and managing Google Cloud Storage buckets.
  - **Service Account Admin** - Required for creating and managing service accounts.
  - **Kubernetes Engine Admin** - Required for creating and managing Google Kubernetes Engine clusters and their resources.

## Installation

### Quick Install with Make

The easiest way to deploy XTDB is using the provided Makefile. This will guide you through the entire process.

```shell
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/Yensid10/xtdb.git
cd xtdb/Google\ Cloud\ Marketplace

# View available commands
make help

# Deploy the complete solution
make setup-all
```

### Manual Installation Steps

If you prefer to follow the installation steps manually, follow this guide.

#### 1. Set up your Google Cloud Project

Ensure you're authenticated with gcloud and have set your project:

```shell
gcloud auth login
gcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT_ID
```

#### 2. Configure VPC Network

You'll need a VPC network for your GKE cluster. You can either create a new one or use an existing one:

```shell
# Create a new VPC network
gcloud compute networks create xtdb-vpc --subnet-mode=custom

# Or use an existing one
```

#### 3. Configure Subnet

Create a subnet within your VPC or use an existing one:

```shell
# Create a new subnet
gcloud compute networks subnets create xtdb-vpc-subnet \
  --network=xtdb-vpc \
  --region=us-central1 \
  --range=10.10.10.0/24

# Or use an existing one
```

#### 4. Create Service Account

Create a service account for XTDB with the necessary permissions:

```shell
gcloud iam service-accounts create xtdb-service-account \
  --display-name="XTDB Service Account"

gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding YOUR_PROJECT_ID \
  --member="serviceAccount:xtdb-service-account@YOUR_PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --role="roles/storage.admin"
```

#### 5. Create GCS Bucket for Storage

```shell
gcloud storage buckets create gs://xtdb-storage-YOUR_PROJECT_ID \
  --location=us-central1 \
  --default-storage-class=STANDARD
```

#### 6. Create GKE Cluster

```shell
gcloud container clusters create xtdb-cluster \
  --zone=us-central1 \
  --network=xtdb-vpc \
  --subnetwork=xtdb-vpc-subnet \
  --num-nodes=1 \
  --machine-type=n2-highmem-2 \
  --disk-size=50 \
  --disk-type=pd-standard \
  --local-ssd-count=1 \
  --workload-pool=YOUR_PROJECT_ID.svc.id.goog

gcloud container node-pools create application-pool \
  --cluster=xtdb-cluster \
  --zone=us-central1 \
  --machine-type=n2-highmem-2 \
  --disk-size=50 \
  --disk-type=pd-standard \
  --local-ssd-count=1 \
  --num-nodes=1

gcloud container clusters get-credentials xtdb-cluster \
  --zone=us-central1
```

#### 7. Setup Kubernetes Namespace and Service Account

```shell
kubectl create namespace xtdb-deployment
kubectl create serviceaccount xtdb-service-account --namespace xtdb-deployment
```

#### 8. Configure Workload Identity

```shell
gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding \
  xtdb-service-account@YOUR_PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
  --role roles/iam.workloadIdentityUser \
  --member "serviceAccount:YOUR_PROJECT_ID.svc.id.goog[xtdb-deployment/xtdb-service-account]"

kubectl annotate serviceaccount xtdb-service-account \
  --namespace xtdb-deployment \
  iam.gke.io/gcp-service-account=xtdb-service-account@YOUR_PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com
```

#### 9. Deploy XTDB

```shell
kubectl apply -f "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/marketplace-k8s-app-tools/master/crd/app-crd.yaml"

# Set deployment parameters
PARAMETERS='{
  "name": "xtdb-kubernetes-deployment",
  "namespace": "xtdb-deployment",
  "xtdb.serviceAccount": "xtdb-service-account",
  "xtdbConfig.gcpProjectId": "YOUR_PROJECT_ID",
  "xtdbConfig.gcpBucket": "xtdb-storage-YOUR_PROJECT_ID"
}'

# Deploy using mpdev
mpdev install --deployer=us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/bcs-test-450214/xtdb-repo/xtdb/deployer:1.0.0 \
  --parameters="$PARAMETERS"
```

## Connecting to XTDB

After deployment, you can connect to XTDB using:

```shell
# Get the service IP
XTDB_IP=$(kubectl get svc xtdb-service --namespace xtdb-deployment -o jsonpath='{.status.loadBalancer.ingress[0].ip}')

# Connect using psql
psql "host=$XTDB_IP port=5432 user=xtdb"
```

Or simply run:

```shell
make connect
```

## Cleanup

To clean up all resources when you're done:

```shell
# Complete cleanup
make cleanup-all

# Or clean up components individually
make cleanup-deployment  # Remove the XTDB Kubernetes deployment
make cleanup-infra       # Remove GKE cluster, GCS bucket, and other GCP resources
```

## Troubleshooting

If you encounter issues during deployment:

1. Check the pod status:
   ```shell
   kubectl get pods -n xtdb-deployment
   ```

2. View pod logs:
   ```shell
   kubectl logs -n xtdb-deployment <pod-name>
   ```

3. Verify that Docker is running on your system before deploying XTDB.

4. Ensure all required GCP APIs are enabled in your project.

